  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>When cyano benzene reacts with hydrochloric acid and water to form benzoic acid which in turn&nbsp;reacts with sodium borohydride to form benzyl alcohol.</p><p>Thus benzy lamine&nbsp;is not formed in option (b). Thus using&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>HCl</mi><mo>/</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>NaBH</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;is not a correct method of the preparation of benzyl amine from cyano benzene.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/f2b2558d-e6d4-4c5d-8d78-4c4ac305f4b5-image.png\" style=\"width: 600px; height: 424px;\" /></p>",
